<p>How have the calls changed over time?</p>
<p>The final chart looks at the total number of roughing-the-passer penalties across the NFL each season since 2014. This helps show whether the league has seen more calls over the years or if the numbers have stayed fairly similar. It also gives us a better idea of how much the penalty has changed over time. With the 2021 season ending with a combined total of 154 roughing the penalties at the end of the year.</p>
<p>The bigger picture</p>
<p>Roughing the passer is always going to be an important penalty because of the protection rules surrounding quarterbacks. At the same time, it can be frustrating for teams and fans when a call changes the direction of a game. Looking at the numbers since 2014 gives us a better idea of which teams have been called the most and how the penalty has changed across the NFL. It shows that there is more to the conversation than just one questionable call during a game.</p>



